The graph rises until the local maximum near \(x\approx -2.5\), then falls until the local minimum near \(x\approx 0.5\), and then rises again.

\[
\boxed{
\begin{aligned}
\text{Increasing on }&(-\infty,-2.5)\ \cup\ (0.5,\infty),\\[2mm]
\text{Decreasing on }&(-2.5,\,0.5).
\end{aligned}
}
\]

The turning-point \(x\)-values are approximations read from the graph; a slightly different estimate such as \(0.6\) or \(1\) would give correspondingly adjusted intervals.
